<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
      Minimal entitlements applied to every CEF Helper.app inside
      Contents/Frameworks/. Chromium's `DeriveCurrentValidationCategory()`
      inspects each helper's entitlements at runtime to identify what kind
      of helper it is (Renderer / GPU / Plugin / Alerts / Main). If the
      helper carries the main-app entitlements (audio-input, camera,
      network.client, etc.), the category derivation fails and the
      embedded webview aborts with errSecCSReqFailed (-67030), leaving
      the window blank.

      These three are what Chromium requires across the helper types:
        - allow-jit + allow-unsigned-executable-memory  : V8 JIT + WASM
        - disable-library-validation                    : load CEF dylibs
      Per-helper-type variation (some only need a subset) is benign for
      the categories Chromium recognises, so we apply the same minimal
      set to all helpers rather than maintaining 5 nearly-identical files.
    -->
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
